{
  "metadata": {
    "name": "Argus Watch",
    "description": "Space Domain Awareness (SDA) exercise. A single MEO observer, 'Argus', must survey its orbital neighbourhood: catalogue ~10 pieces of debris drifting through its field of view at different times, and detect, image, and identify a co-orbital rogue satellite, 'SPECTRE'. SPECTRE hides among the debris but betrays itself with a distinctive RF signature (custom antenna pattern + off-nominal frequency) detectable by Argus' EM Sensor, and a painted callsign confirmable with the optical Camera / CCD. The observer carries an optical Camera and a co-located Charge Coupled Device (CCD) so operators can compare full-frame optical imagery with the low-noise CCD sensor on the same boresight. No scripting required — the rogue team auto-pings, so its transmitter emits continuously; debris are passive orbital objects."
  },
